title:loadPhase
---
//when we declare new variable VSCode automatically designates a type, there's no need to hand-code a type.
<<declare $dialogPhase = "">>
<<declare $visitedYet = false>>
<<dialogPhaseSetter NPC>>
<<if $dialogPhase == "start">>
<<jump Start>>
<<elseif $dialogPhase == "quest_taken">>
<<jump quest_taken_return>>
<<elseif $dialogPhase == "quest_complete">>
<<jump quest_complete>>
<<elseif $dialogPhase == "quest_complete_return">>
<<jump quest_complete_return>>
<<else>>
NPC: I don't know what to do. This is an error debug message. Fix your shit.
<<endif>>
===

title: Start
---
<<set $visitedYet to true>>
<<cam_move NPC_Cam_Rig "npc">>
NPC: Hi there, good to see you.
NPC: Not a lot of people come into my house uninvited.
NPC: But that's OK, I'm pretty chill.
NPC: While you're here, I actually need some help.
NPC: Can you help me?
<<cam_move NPC_Cam_Rig "pc">>
    ->I can help.
        <<dialogPhaseGetter NPC "quest_taken">>
        <<cam_move NPC_Cam_Rig "return">>
    ->Not right now.
        <<cam_move NPC_Cam_Rig "return">>
===
title:quest_taken_return
---
<<cam_move NPC_Cam_Rig "npc">>
NPC: Good to see you again! Did you do the thing I asked you to do?
    <<cam_move NPC_Cam_Rig "pc">>
    ->Nope.
        <<cam_move NPC_Cam_Rig "return">>
===
title:quest_complete
---
<<if $visitedYet == false>>
<<set $visitedYet to true>>
NPC: Oh! Look what you got there, it's just the thing I needed.
NPC: Can I take that off your hands, I really need it!
    ->Sure!
        <<dialogPhaseGetter NPC "quest_complete_return">>
        NPC: Thanks pal.
<<else>>
NPC: Hey again, did you get the thing I asked for?
    ->Sure did!
        <<dialogPhaseGetter NPC "quest_complete_return">>
        OMG, tysm.
<<endif>>
===
title:quest_complete_return
---
NPC: Thanks again for your help. I love you.
===